  The name and the type are the client's word and nothing more. The name is
  cut down to its last piece, so it is never a path, and that is all that is
  done to it: it may still begin with a dot, or be the name of a file that
  is there already. Keep what is uploaded under a name of your own making.
  The type says nothing certain about the bytes.
